{# Demonstrating template for the diagram() template function (Feature f161h).

   The diagram() function lets templates render diagrams whose source
   comes from frontmatter, a layout context, or a shared file --
   places the [diagram] shortcode (which lives in markdown content)
   cannot reach.

   This partial shows two usage shapes:
     1. A live rendered diagram from a hardcoded inline source, so
        theme authors can verify their CSS targets the diagram-wrapper
        classes consistently regardless of which author path emitted
        the SVG.
     2. A frontmatter-driven render, gated on the page-level meta
        field so it stays inert when the page doesn't supply a
        diagram.

   Usage in another template:
       {% include "partials/diagram-fn-example.html.jinja" %}

   Both forms route through the same RenderDispatcher and
   DiagramCache as fenced blocks and the [diagram] shortcode, so the
   rendered SVG is byte-identical for the same source. #}

<section class="diagram-fn-example">
  <h3>Diagram template function example</h3>
  <p>
    The <code>diagram()</code> template function renders a diagram
    inline from a Jinja expression. Use it when the source belongs in
    the template (or in frontmatter) rather than in the page body:
  </p>

  {# Live demonstration: the function actually renders here at build /
     serve time, so this section provides theme authors with a visible
     reference SVG to style. #}
  {{ diagram("mermaid",
             "flowchart LR\n  Author --> Template\n  Template --> SVG",
             caption="Author path: template function",
             alt="A flow showing author content rendered through a template into SVG") }}

  {# Frontmatter-driven path (Feature f045): when a page sets
     `architecture_diagram` in its frontmatter the function picks it up
     here. Inert when unset so the partial is safe to include
     unconditionally. #}
  {% if page.custom.architecture_diagram %}
  <h4>Page architecture (from frontmatter)</h4>
  {{ diagram("mermaid", page.custom.architecture_diagram,
             caption=page.custom.architecture_diagram_caption,
             alt=page.custom.architecture_diagram_alt) }}
  {% endif %}
</section>
